Author:     welpy-cw <h.w.forms@arcor.de>
AuthorDate: Fri May 8 10:01:20 2026 +0000
Commit:     welpy-cw <h.w.forms@arcor.de>
CommitDate: Fri May 8 10:01:20 2026 +0000

    Bug 1913385 - Fix phantom thread twisties during cross-window deletions. r=tobyp

    This patch fixes a UI desynchronization bug where deleting a hidden child
    message in one window leaves a dead "has children" twisty on the parent
    message in other background windows.

    When a message is deleted, the Mork database fires an `OnHdrDeleted`
    notification to all active views. In `nsMsgDBView::OnHdrDeleted`, the base
    class successfully intercepted the deletion of hidden children and called
    `NoteChange` on the thread root, but failed to actually update the visual
    flags if the thread was reduced to a single orphan message.

    Changes:
    * Modified the threaded fallback block in `nsMsgDBView::OnHdrDeleted` to
      check the thread's remaining child count.
    * If the deletion leaves the parent thread as a single-message orphan (<= 1),
      it now dynamically strips the `MSG_VIEW_FLAG_ISTHREAD`, `nsMsgMessageFlags::Elided`,
      and `MSG_VIEW_FLAG_HASCHILDREN` flags to ensure the UI correctly flattens.
    * Extended `browser_deletionFromThreads.js` with `test_cross_window_phantom_twisty`
      to guarantee the `HASCHILDREN` twisty is properly stripped when a hidden child
      is deleted in a separate foreground tab.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D298957

